    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #326\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed the review-feedback commit (`8f93821`) to the existing branch `bb/relay-120-agent-runtime-07-08-enforce-daily-and-thr_rinjgbeb3b`, which already backs open PR #326.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements #120: enforces daily and monthly AI budgets before every gateway provider call, and adds the seam for routing pi through the gateway.\n\n- Registers the AI gateway as pi's provider `baseUrl` for `anthropic`/`openai` via `registerPiProviders()` (agent-runtime), intended to be called once at process startup by the future `services/semprec-agents` composition root (which doesn't exist in this repo yet).\n- Adds `dailyBudgetUsd` (default 50) and nullable `monthlyBudgetUsd` (default uncapped) to System Settings, seeded fresh via `seedSystem.ts` and backfilled onto existing installs via migration `0019_settings_ai_budgets.sql`.\n- `assertWithinBudget` in the AI gateway checks calendar-day and calendar-month spend from `ai_gateway_calls` in one query before each provider call, computed against the system's configured timezone (not UTC), and rejects the call with `BudgetExceededError` if either non-null cap is already reached — driving the originating `agent_run` to `status='error'` when called within a run, or rejecting cleanly with no `agent_runs` mutation otherwise.\n- Check-then-act with no locking, per the issue's accepted imprecision.\n\nAddressed CI code-review feedback from this PR's earlier round: fixed the blocking timezone-correctness issue in the spend query, and both non-blocking suggestions (independent per-key migration backfill guards, simplified test helper).\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Full build (`pnpm run build`) — all packages compile\n- [x] Unit tests — 83/83 passed\n- [x] Integration tests — 484/485 passed; the one failure (`propertyTypeMigration.test.ts` concurrency case, unrelated module) passed in isolation, confirming pre-existing flakiness\n- [x] E2E tests — 5/5 passed\n- [x] Dependency-cruiser boundary check — no violations\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
