    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #326\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully — but I want to flag something important: **PR #326 was already merged** (into `develop`, via merge commit `3c2c92f`) before this push. It merged everything through my first review-fix commit (`8f93821`), which is now part of `develop`.\n\nSince GitHub auto-deletes branches on merge, `bb/relay-120-agent-runtime-07-08-enforce-daily-and-thr_rinjgbeb3b` no longer existed on the remote — my push just recreated it (`git push` reported \"new branch\"). It now contains exactly one commit that isn't yet in `develop`: `62c4642` (\"fetch budgets and timezone in one query\"), the second review-fix from this conversation. That means Relay will likely open a **new** pull request comparing this branch to `develop`, whose diff will just be that one small, already-tested commit — not a duplicate of #326's content.\n\nBranch pushed: `bb/relay-120-agent-runtime-07-08-enforce-daily-and-thr_rinjgbeb3b`\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to merged PR #326 (#120): addresses one more low-priority code-review suggestion that came in after the PR was merged.\n\n`assertWithinBudget` in the AI gateway was calling `getAiBudgets` and `getSystemTimezone` separately, each re-resolving the settings database id and re-reading the settings row (4 round-trips instead of 1, and not atomic against concurrent settings writes). This adds `getAiBudgetsWithTimezone`, which reads the settings row once and derives both the budget caps and the timezone from that single snapshot, then updates the gateway to use it.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Full build — all packages compile\n- [x] Unit tests — 83/83 passed\n- [x] Integration tests — 485/485 passed\n- [x] E2E tests — 5/5 passed\n- [x] Dependency-cruiser boundary check — no violations\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
